{"name":"Tirol","hex":"#9e915c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tirol","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of Tyrol:\nA state in western Austria\nA geographic region in Central Europe including the state of Tyrol in Austria and the regions of South Tyrol and Trentino in Italy","A state in western Austria"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tirol"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tirol (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Tirol was an Irish-bred, British-trained Thoroughbred racehorse and sire. In a racing career that lasted from July 1989 to September 1990 he ran nine times in Britain, Ireland and France. Beginning in September 1989, he won five consecutive races, culminating the following spring with successes in the Classic 2000 Guineas at Newmarket and the Irish 2,000 Guineas at the Curragh. After two defeats later in 1990 Tirol was retired to stud, where he had some success as a sire of winners. He died in India in 2007."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tirol_(horse)","wikidata":"Q7809259"},{"title":"Tyrol","blocks":[{"text":"Tyrol is a historical region in the Alps of Northern Italy and western Austria. The area was historically the core of the County of Tyrol, part of the Holy Roman Empire, Austrian Empire and Austria-Hungary, from its formation in the 12th century until 1919."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Flag_of_Tirol_and_Upper_Austria.svg/330px-Flag_of_Tirol_and_Upper_Austria.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyrol","wikidata":"Q153809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Eurorregi%C3%B3n_Tirol-Tirol_del_Sur-Trentino.png/330px-Eurorregi%C3%B3n_Tirol-Tirol_del_Sur-Trentino.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Eurorregi%C3%B3n_Tiro